{% extends "layout/gates.twig" %}

{# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   THE STAND APPLICATION.

   Two shapes, one page. A signed-in vendor sees only the questions that are about this
   event; a new applicant is asked who they are as well, and the account is created in the
   same request as the application — splitting them produces accounts belonging to people
   who never finished applying.

   ── WHAT THE REBUILD FIXED, AND WHY EACH ONE WAS COSTING APPLICATIONS ───────

   IT LOOKED LIKE A CHECKOUT. Three prices and a submit button, and nothing anywhere
   saying that applying is free. Somebody reading "₦95,000" beside "Create account and
   apply" has every reason to think they are about to be charged, and the ones who are not
   sure close the tab. It now says so, twice, in the places a person is deciding.

   THE STAND LIST RAN TOGETHER. Name, size, category, availability and description were
   one line of mixed weights, and the price — `margin-left:auto` inside a flex whose middle
   child grew — wrapped underneath instead of sitting to the right of it. Five facts of
   four different kinds, presented as a paragraph. Each now has a fixed position, and the
   price is in the same mono column on every row so three of them can be compared down a
   page rather than read one at a time.

   THE CAC FIELD WAS ALWAYS THERE. An individual met a required-looking field for a number
   they do not have, under help text explaining that they should leave it empty — which is
   the sentence that makes a person borrow somebody else's. It is now revealed by the
   answer to "business or individual", with `:has()` written so that an engine WITHOUT
   `:has()` shows both fields rather than hiding one: degraded, it is exactly the old page,
   and no route is ever unfillable.

   NOBODY KNEW WHAT THEY WOULD NEED. The certificates were named in the flash message
   AFTER applying. They are the reason an application sits incomplete, and where
   applications are otherwise equal the tiebreak is whoever became complete first — so
   knowing them is the difference between finishing today and finishing in a fortnight.
   They are now listed before the questions, and they change with the entity answer,
   resolved from `PartnerOrg::vendorDocuments` so the form and the completeness check
   cannot drift apart.

   THERE WAS NO SHAPE. Three cards with headings and no sense of how long the thing was.
   It is now four numbered sections with the last one being what happens after — which is
   the question somebody is holding while they fill in the third.

   ── AND WHAT DID NOT CHANGE ─────────────────────────────────────────────────

   Every field name, every `old` value, the single POST, and the first question still being
   business-or-person as a visible radio pair rather than a dropdown: an individual who
   never sees "individual" concludes the form is not for them and closes the tab.
   ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── #}

{% block head_styles %}
<style nonce="{{ csp_nonce }}">
  /* ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     The same system as the Help Centre, the donations page and the ticket:
     paper ground, hairline rules, mono micro-labels, one gold accent, emerald
     reserved for the action.
     ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */
  body[data-page="stands"]{
    --ap-paper:#f0f2f2;
    --ap-card:#ffffff;
    --ap-cream:#f6f2e6;
    --ap-ink:#10292C;
    --ap-ink-2:#4a5256;                 /* 6.6:1 on paper */
    --ap-mute:#626a6e;                  /* 4.7:1 on paper — the floor */
    --ap-line:rgba(16,41,44,.12);
    --ap-line-2:rgba(16,41,44,.22);
    --ap-gold:#f3b416;
    --ap-gold-ink:#745001;              /* 6.1:1 on paper */
    --ap-green:#237b22;
    --ap-green-dark:#12481d;
    --ap-r:14px;
    --ap-r-sm:4px;

    background:var(--ap-paper); color:var(--ap-ink);
  }
  .ap{ max-width:760px; margin:0 auto;
    padding:clamp(20px,4vw,36px) var(--ag-gutter,32px) clamp(56px,7vw,88px); }

  .ap-kick{ display:block; font-family:var(--ag-font-mono,monospace); font-size:10.5px;
    font-weight:700; letter-spacing:.24em; text-transform:uppercase; color:var(--ap-gold-ink); }

  .ap-back{ display:inline-flex; align-items:center; gap:7px; min-height:32px;
    font-family:var(--ag-font-mono,monospace); font-size:10.5px; font-weight:700;
    letter-spacing:.18em; text-transform:uppercase; color:var(--ap-mute);
    text-decoration:none; }
  .ap-back:hover{ color:var(--ap-ink); }
  .ap-back:focus-visible{ outline:3px solid var(--ap-green); outline-offset:3px; }

  .ap-head h1{ margin:12px 0 0; font-family:var(--ag-font-display,Georgia,serif);
    font-weight:800; font-size:clamp(1.9rem,4.4vw,2.6rem); line-height:1.04;
    letter-spacing:-.03em; color:var(--ap-ink); text-wrap:balance; }
  .ap-head p{ margin:14px 0 0; max-width:56ch; font-size:15.5px; line-height:1.65;
    color:var(--ap-ink-2); text-wrap:pretty; }
  .ap-head b{ color:var(--ap-ink); font-weight:700; }

  /* Applying is free, and the page is full of prices. Said at the top, where the
     decision to start is made, and again beside the button, where the decision to
     finish is. Neither is a footnote. */
  .ap-free{ display:flex; align-items:flex-start; gap:11px; margin-top:20px;
    padding:14px 16px; border-radius:var(--ap-r-sm); background:var(--ap-cream);
    font-size:13.5px; line-height:1.6; color:var(--ap-ink-2); }
  .ap-free svg{ flex:none; margin-top:2px; color:var(--ap-gold-ink); }
  .ap-free b{ color:var(--ap-ink); font-weight:700; }

  /* ── the numbered sections ─────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .ap-sec{ margin-top:clamp(34px,5vw,52px); }
  .ap-sec__h{ display:grid; grid-template-columns:34px minmax(0,1fr);
    column-gap:clamp(12px,2vw,18px); align-items:baseline;
    padding-bottom:14px; border-bottom:1px solid var(--ap-line-2); }
  .ap-sec__n{ font-family:var(--ag-font-mono,monospace); font-size:11px; font-weight:700;
    letter-spacing:.14em; color:var(--ap-gold-ink); }
  .ap-sec__h h2{ margin:0; font-family:var(--ag-font-display,Georgia,serif); font-weight:700;
    font-size:clamp(1.2rem,2.4vw,1.5rem); line-height:1.2; letter-spacing:-.02em;
    color:var(--ap-ink); }
  .ap-sec__h p{ margin:8px 0 0; max-width:58ch; font-size:14px; line-height:1.65;
    color:var(--ap-ink-2); text-wrap:pretty; }
  .ap-sec__b{ margin-top:20px; }

  /* ── the stand chooser ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
     Every fact in a fixed position, and the price in a mono column that lines up
     down the page — because the reader is comparing three of them, not reading
     one. The whole row is the label, so the target is the row and not a 13px
     circle: WCAG 2.5.8 is a floor here, not the goal. */
  .ap-stand{ display:grid; grid-template-columns:20px minmax(0,1fr) auto;
    column-gap:14px; row-gap:8px; align-items:start; padding:18px 16px;
    border:1px solid var(--ap-line-2); border-radius:var(--ap-r-sm);
    margin-bottom:10px; cursor:pointer; background:var(--ap-card); }
  .ap-stand:hover{ border-color:var(--ap-ink); }
  .ap-stand:has(input:checked){ border-color:var(--ap-ink);
    box-shadow:inset 0 0 0 1px var(--ap-ink); background:var(--ap-cream); }
  .ap-stand:focus-within{ outline:3px solid var(--ap-green); outline-offset:2px; }
  .ap-stand input{ margin-top:3px; width:18px; height:18px; accent-color:var(--ap-green-dark); }
  .ap-stand__n{ font-family:var(--ag-font-display,Georgia,serif); font-weight:700;
    font-size:1.08rem; line-height:1.25; letter-spacing:-.01em; color:var(--ap-ink); }
  /* NOT uppercased. `text-transform` reaches the units too, and this line quotes
     physical dimensions: it rendered `1.8 × 0.75 M` and `9 M²`, and a capital M is
     not the metre. Mono at .1em tracking carries the same micro-label weight in
     sentence case, where the category names are correct English as well. */
  .ap-stand__meta{ display:block; margin-top:5px; font-family:var(--ag-font-mono,monospace);
    font-size:10.5px; font-weight:700; letter-spacing:.1em;
    color:var(--ap-mute); }
  /* Never colour alone: the word says "full" and the word says how many are left. */
  .ap-stand__left{ color:var(--ap-green-dark); }
  .ap-stand__full{ color:#8a2b18; }
  .ap-stand__d{ grid-column:2 / -1; margin:0; font-size:13.5px; line-height:1.6;
    color:var(--ap-ink-2); }
  .ap-stand__p{ grid-column:3; grid-row:1; text-align:right; white-space:nowrap;
    font-family:var(--ag-font-mono,monospace); font-weight:700; font-size:1rem;
    font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums; color:var(--ap-ink); }
  /* `white-space:normal`, and a measure. The price cell is `nowrap` so a figure never
     breaks across a line, and the deposit note inherited it — so a 28-character sentence
     became one unbreakable run, the third column grew to fit it, and the meta line in the
     middle column was squeezed until "step-free" broke in half. */
  .ap-stand__dep{ display:block; margin-top:5px; margin-left:auto; max-width:15ch;
    white-space:normal; font-family:var(--ag-font-body,sans-serif); font-size:11.5px;
    font-weight:400; line-height:1.45; letter-spacing:0; color:var(--ap-mute); }
  .ap-stand.is-full{ background:var(--ap-paper); }
  .ap-stand.is-full .ap-stand__n{ color:var(--ap-ink-2); }

  /* ── the entity pair ───────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .ap-pick{ display:grid; grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr; gap:10px; }
  .ap-pick label{ display:grid; grid-template-columns:18px minmax(0,1fr); column-gap:11px;
    align-items:start; padding:16px; border:1px solid var(--ap-line-2);
    border-radius:var(--ap-r-sm); cursor:pointer; background:var(--ap-card); }
  .ap-pick label:hover{ border-color:var(--ap-ink); }
  .ap-pick label:has(input:checked){ border-color:var(--ap-ink);
    box-shadow:inset 0 0 0 1px var(--ap-ink); background:var(--ap-cream); }
  .ap-pick label:focus-within{ outline:3px solid var(--ap-green); outline-offset:2px; }
  .ap-pick input{ margin-top:3px; width:18px; height:18px; accent-color:var(--ap-green-dark); }
  .ap-pick b{ display:block; font-size:14.5px; font-weight:700; color:var(--ap-ink); }
  .ap-pick small{ display:block; margin-top:5px; font-size:12.5px; line-height:1.55;
    color:var(--ap-ink-2); }

  /* ── what you will be asked to upload ──────────────────────────────────────
     Both lists are rendered; `:has()` hides the one that does not apply. Written
     as HIDE-THE-OTHER rather than show-the-right-one so that an engine without
     `:has()` shows both — which is more information than the old page gave, never
     less, and never a route somebody cannot complete. */
  .ap-docs{ margin-top:18px; padding:18px 20px; border-radius:var(--ap-r-sm);
    background:var(--ap-cream); }
  .ap-docs h3{ margin:0; font-family:var(--ag-font-mono,monospace); font-size:10.5px;
    font-weight:700; letter-spacing:.22em; text-transform:uppercase; color:var(--ap-gold-ink); }
  .ap-docs ul{ margin:12px 0 0; padding:0; list-style:none; }
  .ap-docs li{ position:relative; padding:0 0 0 22px; font-size:14px; line-height:1.6;
    color:var(--ap-ink); }
  .ap-docs li + li{ margin-top:7px; }
  .ap-docs li::before{ content:""; position:absolute; left:2px; top:.62em; width:8px;
    height:8px; border-radius:50%; border:1.5px solid var(--ap-gold-ink); }
  .ap-docs p{ margin:12px 0 0; max-width:56ch; font-size:12.5px; line-height:1.6;
    color:var(--ap-ink-2); }
  .ap-f:has(#apEntBusiness:checked) .ap-docs--ind{ display:none }
  .ap-f:has(#apEntIndividual:checked) .ap-docs--biz{ display:none }
  /* And the CAC field, by the same rule and in the same direction. */
  .ap-f:has(#apEntIndividual:checked) .ap-cac{ display:none }

  /* ── fields ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .ap-grid{ display:grid; grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr; gap:20px 18px; }
  /* 11px, not the 9.5px the decorative kickers use. This is the primary label of a
     required field on a form somebody fills in once — it is read rather than glanced at,
     and uppercase mono at 9.5px with .22em tracking is a caption, not a label. */
  .ap-field label{ display:block; font-family:var(--ag-font-mono,monospace); font-size:11px;
    font-weight:700; letter-spacing:.18em; text-transform:uppercase; color:var(--ap-ink-2);
    margin-bottom:8px; }
  .ap-field label em{ font-style:normal; color:var(--ap-mute); }
  .ap-f input[type=text], .ap-f input[type=email], .ap-f input[type=tel],
  .ap-f input[type=password], .ap-f textarea{
    width:100%; box-sizing:border-box; padding:0 14px; min-height:48px;
    border:1px solid var(--ap-line-2); border-radius:var(--ap-r-sm);
    font-family:inherit; font-size:16px; background:var(--ap-card); color:var(--ap-ink);
    outline:none; transition:border-color .12s; }
  .ap-f textarea{ padding:13px 14px; line-height:1.6; resize:vertical; }
  .ap-f input:focus, .ap-f textarea:focus{ border-color:var(--ap-green);
    box-shadow:0 0 0 3px rgba(35,123,34,.16); }
  .ap-field small{ display:block; margin-top:7px; font-size:12.5px; line-height:1.55;
    color:var(--ap-mute); }
  .ap-wide{ grid-column:1 / -1; }

  .ap-check{ display:grid; grid-template-columns:18px minmax(0,1fr); column-gap:11px;
    align-items:start; padding:14px 0; cursor:pointer; }
  .ap-check + .ap-check{ border-top:1px solid var(--ap-line); }
  .ap-check input{ margin-top:2px; width:18px; height:18px; accent-color:var(--ap-green-dark); }
  .ap-check b{ display:block; font-size:14.5px; font-weight:600; color:var(--ap-ink); }
  .ap-check small{ display:block; margin-top:5px; font-size:12.5px; line-height:1.55;
    color:var(--ap-ink-2); }
  .ap-checks{ border-top:1px solid var(--ap-line-2); }

  /* #8a2b18 on #fdecea is 6.4:1. An error message that fails contrast is not an
     error message. */
  .ap-err{ background:#fdecea; border:1px solid #f3c4bd; color:#8a2b18;
    border-radius:var(--ap-r-sm); padding:14px 16px; font-size:14.5px; line-height:1.6;
    margin-top:22px; }
  .ap-err b{ font-weight:700; }

  /* ── what happens next, and the submit ────────────────────────────────── */
  .ap-next{ margin-top:20px; }
  .ap-next li{ display:grid; grid-template-columns:26px minmax(0,1fr); column-gap:12px;
    align-items:baseline; padding:14px 0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--ap-line);
    font-size:14px; line-height:1.65; color:var(--ap-ink-2); }
  .ap-next{ list-style:none; margin:20px 0 0; padding:0;
    border-top:1px solid var(--ap-line-2); }
  .ap-next b{ color:var(--ap-ink); font-weight:700; }
  .ap-next span{ font-family:var(--ag-font-mono,monospace); font-size:11px; font-weight:700;
    letter-spacing:.14em; color:var(--ap-gold-ink); }

  .ap-go{ display:inline-flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center; min-height:52px;
    margin-top:28px; padding:0 30px; border:0; border-radius:var(--ag-r-pill,999px);
    background:var(--ap-green-dark); color:#fff; font-family:inherit; font-weight:700;
    font-size:15.5px; cursor:pointer; }
  .ap-go:hover{ background:#0d3716; }
  .ap-go:focus-visible{ outline:3px solid var(--ap-green); outline-offset:3px; }
  .ap-note{ margin-top:14px; max-width:58ch; font-size:13px; line-height:1.65;
    color:var(--ap-mute); }

  .ap-empty{ padding:22px 0; font-size:14.5px; line-height:1.65; color:var(--ap-ink-2); }

  @media (max-width:640px){
    .ap-grid, .ap-pick{ grid-template-columns:1fr; }
    /* The price moves under the name rather than off the right edge of a 320px
       row: at that width the third column squeezes the name to two words a line. */
    .ap-stand{ grid-template-columns:20px minmax(0,1fr); }
    .ap-stand__p{ grid-column:2; grid-row:auto; text-align:left; }
    /* The note is pushed to the right of a right-aligned column above this width. Left
       of a left-aligned one it has to come back, or it floats away from its own figure. */
    .ap-stand__dep{ margin-left:0; max-width:none; }
  }
</style>
{% endblock %}

{% block content %}
<div class="ap">

  <div class="ap-head">
    <a class="ap-back" href="/events/{{ event.slug }}/stands">
      <svg width="13" height="13" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M19 12H5M11 18l-6-6 6-6"/></svg>
      The call and its terms
    </a>
    <span class="ap-kick" style="margin-top:16px">Stand application</span>
    <h1>Apply to trade at {{ event.title }}</h1>
    {# The date, WRITTEN OUT. `2026-09-01 08:16` is a database value; a person deciding
       whether they have time reads a day and a month. #}
    <p>Applications close <b>{{ call.closes_at|date('l j F Y') }}</b>, at
      {{ call.closes_at|date('g:i a') }}. Everything that decides your application was
      published on the call, and nothing below is scored on how quickly you fill it in.</p>

    <p class="ap-free">
      <svg aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M12 2 4 5v6c0 5 3.4 9.7 8 11 4.6-1.3 8-6 8-11V5l-8-3Z"/><path d="m9 12 2 2 4-4"/></svg>
      <span><b>Applying costs nothing.</b> The prices below are what a stand costs if you
        are offered one and accept it. Nothing is taken today, and no card details are
        asked for anywhere on this form.</span>
    </p>
  </div>

  {% if error %}
    <div class="ap-err" role="alert"><b>That did not go through.</b> {{ error }}</div>
  {% endif %}

  <form method="post" action="/events/{{ event.slug }}/stands/apply" class="ap-f">
    <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrf_token }}">

    {# ── 01 · WHICH STAND ─────────────────────────────────────────────────── #}
    <section class="ap-sec">
      <div class="ap-sec__h">
        <span class="ap-sec__n" aria-hidden="true">01</span>
        <div>
          <h2>Which stand</h2>
          <p>One application per stand type. Applying for two different types is fine if you
            would take either — apply again once this one is in.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="ap-sec__b">
        <fieldset style="border:0;padding:0;margin:0">
          <legend class="sr-only">Choose a stand type</legend>
          {% for c in capacity %}
            <label class="ap-stand{% if c.left == 0 %} is-full{% endif %}">
              <input type="radio" name="stand_type_id" value="{{ c.type.id }}" required
                     {% if old.stand_type_id is defined and old.stand_type_id == c.type.id %}checked{% endif %}>
              <span>
                <span class="ap-stand__n">{{ c.type.name }}</span>
                <span class="ap-stand__meta">
                  {{ c.size }} · {{ categories[c.type.category]|default(c.type.category) }} ·
                  {% if c.left > 0 %}<span class="ap-stand__left">{{ c.left }} of {{ c.quota }} still open</span>
                  {%- else %}<span class="ap-stand__full">All {{ c.quota }} held · waiting list</span>{% endif %}
                  {%- if c.type.includes_power %} · Power included{% endif %}
                  {%- if c.type.step_free %} · Step-free{% endif %}
                </span>
              </span>
              <span class="ap-stand__p">₦{{ c.type.price_naira|number_format }}
                {% if c.type.deposit_naira > 0 %}
                  <span class="ap-stand__dep">₦{{ c.type.deposit_naira|number_format }} deposit
                    on acceptance</span>
                {% endif %}
              </span>
              {% if c.type.description %}<span class="ap-stand__d">{{ c.type.description }}</span>{% endif %}
              {% if c.left == 0 %}
                <span class="ap-stand__d">You can still apply. If a place comes free the
                  longest-waiting applicant is offered it first.</span>
              {% endif %}
            </label>
          {% else %}
            <p class="ap-empty">Nothing is on offer for this event yet. The call lists what
              will be, as soon as it is published.</p>
          {% endfor %}
        </fieldset>
      </div>
    </section>

    {# ── 02 · WHO IS APPLYING ─────────────────────────────────────────────── #}
    {% if org %}
      <section class="ap-sec">
        <div class="ap-sec__h">
          <span class="ap-sec__n" aria-hidden="true">02</span>
          <div>
            <h2>Applying as {{ org.name }}</h2>
            <p>You are signed in, so we already have your details. If anything has changed,
              update it on your <a href="/org">dashboard</a> before the call closes — it is
              what the eligibility check reads.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
    {% else %}
      <section class="ap-sec">
        <div class="ap-sec__h">
          <span class="ap-sec__n" aria-hidden="true">02</span>
          <div>
            <h2>Who is applying</h2>
            <p>You do not need to be a registered company to trade at our events. Most of the
              people who do are not.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="ap-sec__b">

          <fieldset style="border:0;padding:0;margin:0">
            <legend class="ap-kick" style="color:var(--ap-mute);margin-bottom:10px">
              Are you a business or an individual?</legend>
            <div class="ap-pick">
              <label>
                <input type="radio" name="entity_type" value="individual" id="apEntIndividual"
                       {% if old.entity_type is not defined or old.entity_type == 'individual' %}checked{% endif %}>
                <span>
                  <b>Individual or sole trader</b>
                  <small>You trade under your own name or a market name, and are not
                    registered at the CAC. We ask for a photo ID instead.</small>
                </span>
              </label>
              <label>
                <input type="radio" name="entity_type" value="business" id="apEntBusiness"
                       {% if old.entity_type is defined and old.entity_type == 'business' %}checked{% endif %}>
                <span>
                  <b>Registered business</b>
                  <small>You have a CAC registration number — RC, BN or IT.</small>
                </span>
              </label>
            </div>
          </fieldset>

          {# ── WHAT YOU WILL BE ASKED TO UPLOAD ──────────────────────────────
             Before the questions, not after the submit. These are what decide whether an
             application is COMPLETE, and completeness is the published tiebreak — so
             somebody who learns here that they need public liability insurance can go and
             get it today instead of finding out in a fortnight. #}
          {% for entity, list in docs %}
            <div class="ap-docs ap-docs--{{ entity == 'individual' ? 'ind' : 'biz' }}">
              <h3>What you will upload · {{ entities[entity]|default(entity) }}</h3>
              <ul>
                {% for label in list %}<li>{{ label }}</li>{% endfor %}
              </ul>
              <p>Not now — you upload these on your dashboard straight after applying. An
                application is not complete until they are all on file and in date, and
                where applications are otherwise equal the tiebreak is whoever became
                complete first.</p>
            </div>
          {% endfor %}

          <div class="ap-grid" style="margin-top:24px">
            <div class="ap-field">
              <label for="apName">Name you trade under</label>
              <input id="apName" name="name" type="text" maxlength="200" required
                     value="{{ old.name|default('') }}" placeholder="Mama Ngozi’s Kitchen">
              <small>This is what appears on the stand list. It can be your own name.</small>
            </div>
            <div class="ap-field">
              <label for="apLegal">Full legal name</label>
              <input id="apLegal" name="legal_name" type="text" maxlength="200" required
                     value="{{ old.legal_name|default('') }}" placeholder="Ngozi Chioma Okafor">
              <small>Your own full name, or the registered name if you are a business. It
                must match the bank account we settle to — we check that with your bank.</small>
            </div>
            {# Revealed by the answer above. See the `:has()` note in the stylesheet: this
               is written to degrade to VISIBLE, never to hidden. #}
            <div class="ap-field ap-cac ap-wide">
              <label for="apCac">CAC number <em>— registered businesses only</em></label>
              <input id="apCac" name="cac_number" type="text" maxlength="60"
                     value="{{ old.cac_number|default('') }}" placeholder="BN1234567">
              <small>Your own RC, BN or IT number. Do not borrow somebody else’s — it puts
                the wrong name on the paperwork and on the money.</small>
            </div>
            <div class="ap-field">
              <label for="apEmail">Email</label>
              <input id="apEmail" name="contact_email" type="email" maxlength="190" required
                     autocomplete="email" value="{{ old.contact_email|default('') }}">
              <small>This becomes your sign-in, and it is where the decision goes.</small>
            </div>
            <div class="ap-field">
              <label for="apPass">Choose a password</label>
              <input id="apPass" name="password" type="password" minlength="12" required
                     autocomplete="new-password">
              <small>At least 12 characters. This sign-in can later request payouts, so it
                is held to a higher bar than a shopping account.</small>
            </div>
            <div class="ap-field">
              <label for="apContact">Contact name <em>— optional</em></label>
              <input id="apContact" name="contact_name" type="text" maxlength="160"
                     autocomplete="name" value="{{ old.contact_name|default('') }}">
              <small>Who will actually be standing at the pitch, if that is somebody else.</small>
            </div>
            <div class="ap-field">
              <label for="apPhone">Phone <em>— optional</em></label>
              <input id="apPhone" name="contact_phone" type="tel" maxlength="40"
                     autocomplete="tel" value="{{ old.contact_phone|default('') }}">
              <small>Only used if something about your pitch has to be settled on the day.</small>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
    {% endif %}

    {# ── 03 · WHAT YOU WILL SELL ──────────────────────────────────────────── #}
    <section class="ap-sec">
      <div class="ap-sec__h">
        <span class="ap-sec__n" aria-hidden="true">03</span>
        <div>
          <h2>What you will sell</h2>
          <p>This is what the panel reads, and it decides which certificates you need — hot
            food and cosmetics carry requirements that a bookstall does not.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="ap-sec__b">
        <div class="ap-field">
          <label for="apSell">Describe your goods</label>
          <textarea id="apSell" name="what_they_sell" rows="5" required
            placeholder="Jollof rice, moi moi and chin chin, cooked on site. Two staff.">{{ old.what_they_sell|default('') }}</textarea>
          <small>A few plain sentences is enough. What you sell, how it is made or served,
            and how many of you there will be.</small>
        </div>

        <div class="ap-checks" style="margin-top:24px">
          <label class="ap-check">
            <input type="checkbox" name="needs_power" value="1"
                   {% if old.needs_power is defined %}checked{% endif %}>
            <span><b>I need mains power at the pitch</b>
              <small>Some stand types include it and say so above. Asking here is how you get
                it on a pitch that does not.</small></span>
          </label>
          <label class="ap-check">
            <input type="checkbox" name="needs_step_free" value="1"
                   {% if old.needs_step_free is defined %}checked{% endif %}>
            <span><b>I need step-free access to the pitch</b>
              <small>Asked here rather than left to chance. Step-free pitches are allocated,
                not improvised on the morning.</small></span>
          </label>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    {# ── 04 · WHAT HAPPENS NEXT ───────────────────────────────────────────
       The question somebody is holding while they fill in section 03, answered before
       they have to press anything. It is also where the tiebreak is stated a second
       time, because it is the one fact that changes what they do this afternoon. #}
    <section class="ap-sec">
      <div class="ap-sec__h">
        <span class="ap-sec__n" aria-hidden="true">04</span>
        <div>
          <h2>What happens after you press it</h2>
        </div>
      </div>
      <ul class="ap-next">
        <li><span aria-hidden="true">01</span>
          <div>{% if org %}Your application is recorded against this call.{% else %}Your
            account is created and you are signed in — one step, not two.{% endif %}</div></li>
        <li><span aria-hidden="true">02</span>
          <div>You land on your dashboard and <b>upload your certificates</b>. The
            application is not complete until they are all on file and in date.</div></li>
        <li><span aria-hidden="true">03</span>
          <div>Eligibility is a rule, not an opinion. If you fail it we say exactly what is
            missing, and you can fix it while the call is still open.</div></li>
        <li><span aria-hidden="true">04</span>
          <div><b>You hear either way, with a reason.</b> If you are offered a stand you have
            {{ offer_hours|default(72) }} hours to accept before the place goes to the
            waiting list.</div></li>
      </ul>

      <button class="ap-go" type="submit">
        {{ org ? 'Submit application' : 'Create account and apply' }}</button>
      <p class="ap-note"><b>Still free.</b> Pressing this does not take a payment and does
        not commit you to a stand — a place is only yours once you are offered one and
        accept it.</p>
    </section>
  </form>
</div>
{% endblock %}
